hey guys  we are going to discuss something else  here other than the most verse in this  video  and that is the dinosaurs that have been  seen in the preview  of jurassic world 3 dominion while the  first two jurassic world movies and  netflix jurassic world camp cretaceous  introduced the concept of hybrid  dinosaurs  such as the indominus rex the indiraptor  and the scorpius rex which were the  antagonists of the first two jurassic  world movies and camp cretaceous  respectively there will be no hybrid  dinosaurs  in this third one instead the film will  focus on dinosaur species that actually  existed  millions of years ago dominion will  feature all new ancient dinos including  a couple that were recently unearthed by  real world paleontologists  so if you're ready let's get down with  the sickness  the preview takes place in both the past  and the present beginning 65 million  years ago during the cretaceous period  with composer michael giattino providing  the music the score  the trailer seems to be like a nature  documentary with us following a group of  dinosaurs as they roam the area  it is serene and tranquil allowing us to  appreciate our planet's natural beauty  before humans arrive  so what we get here are the  dreadnoughtus the queso cordless  the oviraptor the nasoceratops the  iguanodon  morris intrepidus and the giganotosaurus  which are seven new dinosaur species  created by the team  at industrial light and magic that have  never been seen before in any previous  jurassic films  and so these dinosaurs in detail are as  follows  the dread notice which is a massive new  sauropod similar to the brachiosaurus  and the bones of this dinosaur were only  discovered in real life  in 2005. then we have the quetzalcoatlus  which has an even bigger and scarier  winged pterosaur  way bigger than pteranodons they are  like tall giraffes  dragon dinos then the nasoceratops which  is similar to a triceratops and  or a cyanoceratops but it has shorter  horns  that protrude from behind its bony  armored plate forward  the feathered morris intrepidus is a  genus of tyrannosaurid  theropod that lived during the late  cretaceous period which is now utah in  the united states  this is the one that looked like a  raptor in the poster but is in fact a  relative of the t-rex  now we also see the iguanodon which were  large bulky herbivores with features  that include large tom spikes which were  possibly used  for defense against predators and  combined with long prehensile fifth  fingers  that were used to forage for food next  the oviraptor  which is a feather dinosaur that is very  similar to the velociraptor but smaller  in scale  and commonly known as the egg thief it  is one of the first dinosaurs with  feathers in the jurassic world franchise  which is more scientifically accurate  and lastly the giganotosaurus which was  one of the largest meat eating dinosaurs  it rome roamed modern-day argentina  during the late cretaceous period  it was even bigger than the t-rex but  smaller than spinosaurus  so in the preview we see a t-rex and a  giganotosaurus fighting in the middle of  the late cretaceous background  and the t-rex is killed after a very  short battle which was kind of shocking  as  even the spinosaurus and the indominus  rex took quite a while to get the  advantage  we then observe the dead t-rex and a  mosquito flying into the t-rex and take  blood from the area surrounding the body  of the t-rex  while also we get a close-up of the  t-rex's eye dilating  so the question is is this the same  amber mosquito  seen on john hammond's staff in the  original jurassic park film  well that is unknown however it is  evident that this is the origin story of  the t-rex we know  and love from jurassic world movies rexy  then in the next scenes we shift to 65  million years later  and now we're following the t-rex in the  present day  as it races through a forest pursued by  people in a helicopter  who are attempting to tranquilize it  with a tranquilizer dot obviously  and the t-rex enters a drive in parking  lot as the race through the forest  continues  causing mayhem as people try to flee the  gigantic dinosaur  of course it is rumored that the  giganotosaurus would be the main  antagonist in the third movie  and so this might lead to another  confrontation and battle  between the t-rex and the giganotosaurus  and then rexy would exact her revenge  and come to think about it they are the  exact ones that fought 65 million years  ago  well maybe clones of them but them  nonetheless  and so that's that what do you think the  movie will be released next year on june  10th  we will also dive in deeper into the  morris intrepidus and the giganotosaurus  in the next videos  so do like for support subscribe to be a  part of the mind cue family  and hit that bell button for regular  updates on new master videos  right here on minecu till the next one  take care fam

